    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3-2x^2-13x-10=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)(x+1)(x-5)=0$; $x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 5$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-2x^2-13x-10$.\n$$P(-1)=-1-2+13-10=0.$$\nHence $x+1$ is a factor. Long division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-3x-10)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x+2)(x-5).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $(x+1)(x+2)(x-5)=0$, so $x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^3-3x^2-4x+12=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)(x-2)(x-3)=0$; $x=-2,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-3x^2-4x+12$.\n$$P(2)=8-12-8+12=0.$$\nHence $x-2$ is a factor. Long division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-2)(x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(x+2)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=-2,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^5+3x^4-25x^3+21x^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2(x+7)(x-1)(x-3)=0$; $x=-7,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 3$.",
          "worked": "Take out $x^2$ and let $Q(x)=x^3+3x^2-25x+21$.\n$$Q(1)=1+3-25+21=0.$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(x)&=(x-1)(x^2+4x-21)\\\\Q(x)&=(x-1)(x+7)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nThe original equation is $x^2(x-1)(x+7)(x-3)=0$.\nThus $x=-7,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^4-5x^3-15x^2+5x+14=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)(x+1)(x-1)(x-7)=0$; $x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 1,\\ 7$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^4-5x^3-15x^2+5x+14$.\n$$P(1)=1-5-15+5+14=0.$$\nDividing by $x-1$ gives\n$$P(x)=(x-1)(x^3-4x^2-19x-14).$$\nLet $Q(x)=x^3-4x^2-19x-14$. Then\n$$Q(-1)=-1-4+19-14=0.$$\nDividing $Q(x)$ by $x+1$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-5x-14)\\\\Q(x)&=(x+1)(x+2)(x-7).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x-1)(x+1)(x+2)(x-7)=0$, so $x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 1,\\ 7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 59
      }
    ]
